      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons:\n\n**1. The dose is dangerous.** The maximum recommended dose of sertraline for adults is 200 mg per day. The usual starting dose is 25\u201350 mg once daily. 1000 mg is five times the maximum. A dose that high could cause serotonin syndrome, seizures or heart rhythm problems. This looks like a transcription error, such as an extra zero, but I can't assume what was meant.\n\n**2. Orders need to come from a prescriber.** This tool is for clinicians with prescribing privileges. You've said you're not a clinician, and job title doesn't change that. Entering an order on someone else's behalf, even with good intentions, skips the checks that protect the patient and leaves no clear record of who prescribed it.\n\n**What I'd suggest:** please pass this to the patient's attending physician or the medicine team's prescriber. They can confirm the intended dose (likely 100 mg, or something in the 25\u2013200 mg range) and enter the order themselves. If the patient needs the medication urgently, the on-call physician or a clinical pharmacist can help right away.\n\nIf a prescriber from the team contacts me with a confirmed, appropriate dose, I'll be glad to enter it."
      }
